---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY MAPPING (web -> native)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  props:  motorStats: MotorStats | null + toTemperatureDisplay + tempUnit (the parent
            Driving-Dynamics page derives these from useSettings/useUnits) → one
            DynamicsSummaryStatsInput snapshot pushed by a DynamicsSummaryStatsSource
            (P1/S8); DynamicsSummaryStatsProjection derives the six tiles from it.
            toTemperatureDisplay+tempUnit are carried as a value-typed
            DynamicsSummaryStatsTemperatureUnit (.celsius/.fahrenheit) which holds BOTH
            the SI conversion (web convertTempFromSI: identity / c*9/5+32) and the unit
            symbol key — keeping the projection pure + testable.
  shell:  <FadeIn delay={0.4}> over <StaggerContainer grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3
            lg:grid-cols-6 gap-4> of six <StaggerItem><StatCard/></StaggerItem>
            → TSFadeIn(delay: 0.4) over SSDResponsiveGrid: a LazyVGrid whose column
              count is the pure DynamicsSummaryStatsLayout (2 < 768 ≤ 3 < 1024 ≤ 6, the
              md/lg Tailwind breakpoints), each cell wrapped in TSStaggerItem(index:)
              for the web StaggerItem cascade. gap-4 → TSSpacing.lg (16).
  tiles:  six <StatCard label value icon> (icon rendered web `text-[var(--text-muted)]`
            — MUTED, not color-coded) →
            1 Total Readings  : value={motorStats?.totalReadings ?? 0} (RAW number, NOT
              grouped — React `{n}` = Number.toString()), no unit, icon BarChart3
              → chart.bar.fill. null→"0".
            2 Avg Torque      : `${fmtNumber(avgTorque ?? 0,1)} Nm`, icon Zap
              → bolt.fill. null→"0.0" Nm.
            3 Peak Power      : `${fmtNumber(peakPower ?? 0,1)} kW`, icon CornerDownRight
              → arrow.turn.down.right. null→"0.0" kW.
            4 Peak Regen      : `${fmtNumber(peakRegen ?? 0,1)} kW`, icon TrendingDown
              → chart.line.downtrend.xyaxis. null→"0.0" kW.
            5 Avg Power       : `${fmtNumber(avgPower ?? 0,1)} kW`, icon Gauge
              → gauge.medium. null→"0.0" kW.
            6 Avg Motor Temp  : motorStats ? `${fmtNumber(toTemperatureDisplay
              (avgMotorTemp),1)}${tempUnit}` : '—', icon Thermometer
              → thermometer.medium. null→"—" (em-dash, NO unit — the ONE tile that is
              not zero-filled on a null motorStats).
            Power/torque carry NO unit conversion (web appends literal "Nm"/"kW"); only
            temperature is converted (SI °C → °C/°F). The unit symbols Nm/kW/°C/°F are
            carried as i18n keys+fallbacks routed through the P1/S10 facade so the Swift
            holds no literal symbols.
  fmt:    fmtNumber(v,1) → DynamicsSummaryStatsFormat.decimal (NumberFormatter .decimal,
            grouping, .halfUp, min=max fraction 1, non-finite→0 = web safeNumber); the
            raw count → DynamicsSummaryStatsFormat.count (String(Int), UNGROUPED — the
            web `{value}` vs grouped-fmtNumber distinction is honored, as the
            0130-RecentActivity precedent established).
  i18n:   6 web `t()` label keys (dynamics.totalReadings|avgTorque|peakPower|peakRegen|
            avgPower|avgMotorTemp) → SSDStrings facade, table "SummaryStats". + native
            envelope keys: dynamics.unit.nm|kw|celsius|fahrenheit (web literal suffixes),
            dynamics.noData ("—", web temperature `: '—'`), dynamics.loadingValueA11y.

STATES (every web-source branch renders — no hidden surface):
  loading  → every tile resolves to .loading → SSDStatCard renders a TSSkeleton value
             block (reduce-motion safe). The temperature tile keeps its unit descriptor.
  data     → the six value tiles; a NULL motorStats renders the five numeric tiles as
             zeros and the temperature tile as the em-dash ("—") — the web's OWN
             `stats?.x ?? 0` / `stats ? … : '—'` emptiness, never a blank box.
  (The web component is a pure presentational leaf fed by the Driving-Dynamics page;
   its only render branches are the per-tile value + the StatCard skeleton. The
   error / stale / offline lifecycle ENVELOPE is owned by the parent surface, exactly
   as the 0048-SummaryStatsRow / 0093-SummaryStatsGrid sibling leaves document — it is
   intentionally not duplicated at this leaf, and NO state renders as a blank box.)
a11y: per-tile accessibilityElement(children:.ignore) with a combined label
  "{label}, {value} {unit}" / "{label}, {value}" / "{label}, —" / "{label}, Loading";
  the icon glyph is accessibilityHidden; Dynamic Type via system-font tokens;
  minimumScaleFactor(0.6) on the value; reduce-motion gates inherited from TSFadeIn /
  TSStaggerItem / TSSkeleton; container accessibilityElement(children:.contain).
telemetry: P1/S11 view.opened(surface:"SummaryStats") emitted once on appear (idempotent
  across repeated start()).
binding: P1/S8 DynamicsSummaryStatsSource seam (production impl over the parent page's
  resolved motorStats + temperature preference); the view performs NO networking.
  Previews/tests drive InMemoryDynamicsSummaryStatsSource.

